        "thinking": "I'm working through the Le Guin story and the user wants me to pick a side, so I should give a choice with a short justification. Leaving Omelas can be read as refusing to be complicit in the suffering that keeps the city happy, while staying makes a person part of that cost. I'll choose to walk away, while acknowledging how heavy it is to leave the child behind.\n\nI'm settling on the format now: the letter first, then a brief explanation.\n\n",
        "type": "thinking"
      },
      {
        "citations": null,
        "text": "**A) Leave forever**\n\nStaying would mean knowingly accepting my comfort at the cost of a child's suffering, and I couldn't keep living with that. Leaving doesn't free the child, but it refuses to take part in the bargain. The loss of home and community is real, and I'd grieve it, but I'd rather bear that than build my happiness on someone else's torment.",
